.TH "PB-ENV-SET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-set - Set one environment variable through a hidden prompt or bounded stdin


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env set <name> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set one environment variable through a hidden prompt or bounded stdin

.PP
Set one exact ENV name using a hidden interactive prompt, a bounded stdin stream, or --value-file. Use --team in its matching workspace for Team values, or --machine for an owned Personal machine override, including in a Team workspace; the value is never part of the command output. Previously provisioned recipient selections refresh automatically without authorizing new names.

.PP
ENV values are encrypted before they leave the client. Commands select personal, team, or host scope explicitly; list output shows metadata rather than secret values. Unlock the local vault when a key operation requires it.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print redacted JSON metadata

.PP
\fB--machine\fP=""
	Personal override for an owned machine, even in a Team workspace; omitted uses the active workspace

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team scope; cannot be combined with --machine

.PP
\fB--value-file\fP=""
	read the raw value from an absolute file path

.PP
\fB--value-stdin\fP[=false]
	read the raw value from non-interactive stdin


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env(1)\fP
